  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Catch it and start again",
  "description": "Play 3 v 3 with keepers on a pitch of roughly 25 × 18 metres, with goals about 3 metres wide. When the keeper has the ball they restart by throwing it out, rolling it, dribbling out or passing. Everyone takes a turn in goal – switch after each goal or every three minutes.\n\nGive the team a bonus point when the keeper catches a shot cleanly, so everyone wants to hold the ball rather than just block it.\n\nWarm-up in pairs: two small goals 3 metres wide stand 5 metres apart. One player throws or shoots, the other catches – or dives – and then you swap. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Keeper: shuffle sideways so you are in line with the ball when the shot comes."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Catch with both hands and bring the ball in to your body."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Restart quickly to a teammate who is free, ideally out wide."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Outfield: stand between the ball and your goal when the other team has it."
    }
  ],
